Cases include positive/negative fractional truncation; zero and negative zero;
+/- (2^32+1), signed 32-bit boundary, and 2^32-1 and 2^32.
This helper uses canonical JS_ToDouble plus ECMA-262 modulo 2^32 semantics;
it does not fake a SpiderMonkey JSContext, JSValue binary layout or GC roots.
This is a numeric compatibility gate only. Full OOJS engine conversion, 101
historical JS_* unresolved symbols, complete link and playability are not done.
